# Portal universal rules

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/08-architecture-standards.md` first. Before changing configuration, inspect the relevant package manifest and `.env.example`.

## Boundaries

- Backend and frontend never cross-import.
- Preserve `/api/v1` contracts and existing public URLs during refactors (route groups must not change URLs).
- Persian UI is RTL and must remain usable on mobile and desktop.
- Keep files under 300 lines, route handlers under 60, and service methods under 80; split growing units.
- Frontend features import other domains only through that domain's public `index.ts`, or via `components/shared`, `components/ui`, `lib`, or `api`.
- Backend new work uses class-based services and repositories; routes stay thin.

## Naming and imports

- Python: `snake_case` functions/files and `PascalCase` classes.
- TypeScript: `camelCase` values and `PascalCase` components/types.
- TypeScript imports: framework, external packages, `@/*`, then relative modules.
- Python imports: standard library, third-party packages, then `app.*`.

## Forbidden

- Secrets, tokens, passwords, databases, uploads, `node_modules`, or build output in Git.
- Hardcoded service origins where an environment variable exists.
- Business logic in FastAPI handlers or Next.js page modules.
- New React Router routes; use Next.js App Router with `(auth)` / `(portal)` / `(admin)` groups.
- Cross-feature private imports (`features/a` → `features/b/screens|components|api|hooks`).
- A second UI system beside vendored shadcn kit primitives in `components/ui`.
- New ORM/query workflows inside FastAPI route modules.
- `console.log`, untyped API payloads, or unexplained TypeScript `any`.
